# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAREFUL: the bundled tool archives (*.tar.xz, *.tar.xz.partNN, *.tar.gz,
# *.tgz, *.nbm) ARE the point of this repository - they are what makes it work
# with no internet. So the usual Java .gitignore, which ignores every archive,
# must NOT be used here. Only build output and local state are ignored below.
#
# Nothing is committed as *.zip or *.jar: some git hosts refuse those types
# outright. Jars travel inside a .tar.xz and land in tools/ at setup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Unpacked tools: produced by scripts/00-setup.sh from the archives in this repo.
tools/

# Everything the scripts write at run time goes to $PERF_OUT (default
# $HOME/perf-out), never into the repository - but ignore it anyway in case
# someone points PERF_OUT here.
perf-out/

# Build output
*.class
target/
build/
out/

# Loose jars/zips must never be committed - the host rejects them. If you are
# repackaging a tool, archive it as .tar.xz instead (see README, Split archives).
*.jar
*.zip

# JVM crash logs
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editors / OS
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
